## Terminology stores

| File | Effect | Reaches packets | In the audit hash |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `glossary/approved.yaml` — `status: {{ approved_status }}` (or absent) | hard per-unit QA gate (`approved-term-missing`; `forbidden` checked in **every** unit) | the entries matching the packet's units | those entries only |
| `glossary/approved.yaml` — `status: {{ reference_status }}` | binding, not gated | same filter | same |
| `glossary/reference.yaml` (status defaults to `{{ reference_status }}`) | binding, not gated; grouped by `kind` (default `{{ default_reference_kind }}`) | same filter | same |
| `status: {{ proposed_status }}` in either file | inert | no | no |
| `glossary/candidates.yaml` | none; undecided entries are listed in the finalize unresolved report, decided ones only counted | no | no |

Matching: `match` is one of {% for mode in term_match_modes %}`{{ mode }}`{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %} (default
`{{ term_match_modes[0] }}`); `aliases` are extra source forms located the same way; `scope` is
`document`, `page:N` or a parent unit id. Source text and entries are both folded before
matching (accents in every written form, ligatures, curly quotes, dash variants, whitespace
runs, case); regex literals are folded too while escapes are kept. An approved entry that
matches no prepared unit is reported once per QA run (`approved-term-never-matched`);
`glossary check` reports the same for reference entries, and `glossary lookup` shows what a
batch, page range or text will receive.

## Audit context and staleness

The shared audit context is exactly these parts, hashed together
(`evidence.audit_context_text`):

